   "source": "# **Uber Supply-Demand Gap Analysis**\n\n##### **Project Type** - EDA (Exploratory Data Analysis)\n##### **Contribution** - Individual\n##### **Team Member 1 -** *(Your Name)*\n\n---\n\n# **Project Summary**\n\nThis project performs an Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) on Uber ride request data collected over 5 days (July 11\u201315, 2016). The dataset contains 6,745 ride requests between the city and the airport. The main objective is to identify the root causes of the supply-demand gap \u2014 situations where riders request a cab but either no cars are available or the driver cancels the trip.\n\nKey findings from this analysis:\n- **Night time (7 PM\u201310 PM)** has the highest number of unfulfilled requests, primarily from the **Airport** side due to \"No Cars Available.\"\n- **Morning and Early Morning (12 AM\u201310 AM)** see the highest driver **cancellations**, mostly from the **City** side, as drivers don't want to make the long airport trip early in the day.\n- The supply-demand gap is significantly larger at the **Airport** (\u22481000 unfulfilled requests) compared to the **City** (\u2248820).\n- **Recommended solutions**: Incentivize drivers with surge/rush-hour pricing during morning slots; introduce dedicated night-shift drivers to cover the airport-to-city demand at night.\n\n# **GitHub Link**\n[https://github.com/yourusername/uber-eda-project](https://github.com/yourusername/uber-eda-project)\n\n# **Problem Statement**\nUber is facing a significant supply-demand gap: many ride requests are going unfulfilled either because no cabs are available or because drivers are cancelling rides. This hurts customer experience and revenue.\n\n#### **Define Your Business Objective**\nTo identify **when** (time of day) and **where** (pickup point: City or Airport) the gap is most severe, understand the **root causes** (cancellations vs. unavailability), and recommend **data-driven solutions** to bridge the gap.\n\n---\n# ***Let's Begin!***"
