   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# Chart 1: Distribution of Trip Status (Pie + Bar)\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n\nstatus_counts = df['Status'].value_counts()\ncolors = ['#2ecc71', '#e74c3c', '#e67e22']\n\n# Pie chart\naxes[0].pie(status_counts, labels=status_counts.index, autopct='%1.1f%%',\n            colors=colors, startangle=140, textprops={'fontsize': 12})\naxes[0].set_title('Trip Status Distribution (Pie)', fontsize=14)\n\n# Bar chart\naxes[1].bar(status_counts.index, status_counts.values, color=colors, edgecolor='black')\naxes[1].set_title('Trip Status Distribution (Bar)', fontsize=14)\naxes[1].set_ylabel('Count')\nfor i, v in enumerate(status_counts.values):\n    axes[1].text(i, v + 30, str(v), ha='center', fontweight='bold')\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "- **Why this chart?** A pie + bar combo gives both proportion and absolute count at a glance.\n- **Insight:** Only **42%** of requests are completed. A massive **58% are unfulfilled** \u2014 39% \"No Cars Available\" and 19% \"Cancelled\". This confirms a critical supply-demand gap.\n- **Business Impact:** Over half of all customers are leaving unsatisfied. This is a direct revenue loss and reputational risk for Uber."
